{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessBoundedCapstone","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiStripGrowth","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MeromorphicPuncturedBounded"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthUniqueness.faddeevPhi_proportional_of_stripGrowth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthUniqueness.faddeevPhi_proportional_of_stripGrowth","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevStripGrowthUniqueness.lean#L39-L72","doc":"**Strip-growth ⇒ proportionality (G5).** For two `FaddeevPhi` solutions at `b`\n(nondegenerate lattice `(b²).im ≠ 0`) that are both `FaddeevPhiStripGrowth` — i.e. comparable\nin modulus to `phiBProd b` — with `Φ₂`'s zeros isolated and the normal-form-vs-ratio identity\nholding off `Φ₂`'s zeros, and the two dense periodicity loci: the solutions are proportional\non `Φ₂`'s nonvanishing locus. The analytic `hbdd` input of the boundedness capstone is\n**derived** here from the strip-growth class, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}